1. Passages quoted from editions
--------------------------------

The data files under jyotirganita/data/, jyotirganita/methods/ and
jyotirganita/regions/ hold short passages quoted from the editions
listed in jyotirganita/data/sources.yaml, each with its page. A passage
from an edition whose `copyright` there is `in-copyright` (among them
the editions and translations by K. S. Shukla, K. V. Sarma and their
co-editors published by Lucknow University, the Indian National Science
Academy, the Vishveshvaranand Vedic Research Institute and the
Kuppuswami Sastri Research Institute) is quoted, with citation, for
scholarly research and review: it records what the edition prints on
the page a datum cites. These passages remain the copyright of their
publishers and are not licensed under the Apache License by this
project. Numbers and rules of the pre-modern texts themselves are the
texts' own content, cited to the edition that witnesses them.

2. Published tables shipped as data
-----------------------------------

The extracts under jyotirganita/data/tables/ and jyotirganita/data/modern/
are taken from the following publications. Each extract records the
file it was taken from and that file's SHA-256 in
jyotirganita/data/sources.yaml.

- IERS Earth orientation series EOP 20 C04 (UT1-UTC, ΔT) and the
  leap-second table Leap_Second.dat of IERS Bulletin C (TAI-UTC),
  International Earth Rotation and Reference Systems Service,
  https://hpiers.obspm.fr/iers/eop/eopc04/ and
  https://hpiers.obspm.fr/iers/bul/bulc/ (fetched 2026-10-09).
  Terms: the publisher's page states no terms of use (read
  2026-10-31). The series is credited here to the IERS Earth
  Orientation Centre.
- IAU 2000A nutation series and IAU 2006 precession, IERS Conventions
  (2010), IERS Technical Note 36, ed. G. Petit and B. Luzum,
  https://iers-conventions.obspm.fr/ (fetched 2026-10-09).
  Terms: the publisher's page states no terms of use (read
  2026-10-31). Credited here to the IERS and its editors.
- IAU 1980 nutation series, IERS Conventions (1996), IERS Technical
  Note 21, ed. D. D. McCarthy. Terms: the publisher's page could not
  be read (2026-10-31); no terms are claimed. Credited here to the IERS
  and its editor.
- ΔT polynomials of F. Espenak and J. Meeus, NASA Goddard Space Flight
  Center, https://eclipse.gsfc.nasa.gov/SEcat5/deltatpoly.html
  (fetched 2026-10-09). Terms: a work of the U.S. Government. The
  NASA eclipse site grants permission to reproduce its data with an
  acknowledgment, given here: Fred Espenak and Jean Meeus, NASA/GSFC.
- ΔT spline of F. R. Stephenson, L. V. Morrison and C. Y. Hohenkerk,
  "Measurement of the Earth's rotation: 720 BC to AD 2015", Proc. R.
  Soc. A 472, 20160404 (2016), supplementary data,
  https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/6998699 (fetched 2026-10-09).
  Terms: the article is published under the Creative Commons
  Attribution License (CC BY 4.0), which permits unrestricted use
  provided the original author and source are credited; they are
  credited here.
- Hipparcos catalogue (ESA 1997, I/239), extract of the one star the
  ayanāṃśas name (Spica, HIP 65474), via VizieR, CDS Strasbourg
  (fetched 2026-10-09). Terms: the CDS licence page could not be read
  (2026-10-31); no terms are claimed. The extract holds only that
  star's catalogue entry, credited here to ESA (1997) and the CDS,
  Strasbourg.
- Precession expressions of J. Vondrák, N. Capitaine and P. Wallace,
  Astronomy & Astrophysics 534, A22 (2011), with its corrigendum.
  Terms: the journal's page could not be read (2026-10-31); no terms
  are claimed. Only the published expressions' coefficients are used,
  credited here to the authors.
- IANA time zone database, release 2025b, https://data.iana.org/
  (fetched 2026-10-08). In the public domain, as its LICENSE file
  states (https://data.iana.org/time-zones/tzdb/LICENSE, read
  2026-10-29).

The JPL planetary ephemerides (DE440, DE441) are not shipped: the user
fetches them from JPL (jyotirganita fetch-kernel).

3. Optional dependency
----------------------

The optional extra `swisseph` installs pyswisseph (Swiss Ephemeris,
AGPL-3.0). It is reserved for cross-check tests of the `extras` tier,
which holds no test in 1.0.0, and nothing in the package imports it. It
is not a dependency of the package.
